    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83286.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "The Times reported Monday that acting Defense Secretary Patrick Shanahan had presented the plan to top national security officials. The plan, according to anonymously cited sources, would be to send up to 120,000 U.S. troops to the region if Iran attacks U.S. forces or continues to accelerate its nuclear program. The plan does not, however, include a land invasion, according to the Times.",
