    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83286.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "I have recently, as many of you know, I think I've recently met with the FBI concerning the election issue mentioned in the Mueller report, which was, I guess, come out a couple weeks ago. And this is for the 2016 election, two Florida counties experienced intrusion into the supervisor of election networks. There was no manipulation or anything, but there was voter data that was able to be gotten. Now that voter data, I think, was public anyways. Nevertheless, those were intrusions. It did not affect any voting or anything like that. So when the FBI will talk about election infrastructure, they include anything that could be in the supervisor of elections. This was something where they had spearfishing Someone clicked on it so someone was able to get access to things but nothing that affected the vote count.",
